          "runnable": true
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Tools At The Prompt",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ip -4 addr show` prints inet 10.0.5.23/24",
            "`ip route get 8.8.8.8` shows the entry LPM chose",
            "`ip route show`: the default via line is 0.0.0.0/0",
            "`ipcalc 192.168.10.37/26` checks hand math, never replaces it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Cloud Reservations Bite",
          "text": "AWS VPC CIDR must be /16-/28 and AWS reserves 5 addresses per subnet, so a /28 gives 11 usable, not 14. Kubernetes caps pods per node with a node pod CIDR."
        },
